+## Stages and artifacts
 
-## Phases
+| Stage | Required outcome |
+| --- | --- |
+| Context | Capture the request, approved design and relevant tracker evidence in `impl/intent.md`; create `2-report.md` and initialize metrics. Ask about material missing/conflicting intent only. |
+| Ceremony | Inspect/reuse or create a local feature branch safely. Delegate authorized tracker setup by state name; local DEV IDs do not imply tracker records. |
+| Plan | Read the active HLD and relevant LLD/code. Prepare numbered steps, meaningful acceptance criteria and actual available checks. Resolve material design/scope choices; persist `1-plan.md`. |
+| Implement | Execute logical steps with observed verification. Add/update tests when useful, choosing unit, integration, load or other types to fit the work and project setup. Test-first work is optional; required checks must pass. Record progress, notes, findings and debt. |
+| Test | Run relevant existing checks, conduct scoped PR review, fix in-scope regressions, rerun affected checks and explicitly verify acceptance criteria. Preserve test evidence. |
+| Document | Audit implementation against HLD, update permanent docs, review consistency, resolve findings, and archive only after closure checks. |
 
-**Router:** `/dev <TICKET> <problem statement>` — runs all six stages in one session, stopping at each boundary for confirmation. Bail out at any point and resume with the individual command. One skill (`dev`) owns all six stages as `references/01-context-gathering.md` … `references/06-document.md`; there is no separate installable skill per stage.
+The approved plan is immutable. New authorized scope uses an explicit addendum.
+Use native Plan Mode when available and respect its write/approval restrictions;
+otherwise prepare a reviewable local plan. No stage assumes a framework, test suite,
+linter or pre-commit hook that the project has not configured.
 
-| Stage                 | Individual command               | What it produces                                                               |
-| ---------------------- | ---------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
-| **Context Gathering** | `/dev context <TICKET> <problem>` | `intent.md` + `2-report.md` (skeleton) + the story folder itself, in `Stories/<TICKET>/impl/` |
-| **Ceremony**          | `/dev ceremony <TICKET>`          | Tracker transitioned to In Progress, feature branch confirmed                 |
-| **Plan**              | `/dev plan <TICKET>`              | `1-plan.md` (immutable) in `Stories/<TICKET>/impl/`; `2-report.md` Progress table populated |
-| **Implement**         | `/dev implement <TICKET>`         | Code commits, one step at a time; findings captured in `2-report.md`           |
-| **Test**              | `/dev test <TICKET>`              | Build + test + lint results; PR review appended to `2-report.md`               |
-| **Document**          | `/dev document <TICKET>`          | Updated READMEs / LLD / Engineering Guide; story archived                      |
+## Human decisions
 
----
+The dev skill's `patterns/approvals.md` owns authorization boundaries. Routine context
+reads, reversible local edits, checks, report updates and stage transitions continue
+within scope. Preserve existing authorization across steps and sessions.
 
-## Invariants
+Pause for material scope/architecture decisions, real risk acceptance or deferral,
+required verification only a human can perform, or an external/destructive action that
+has not been authorized. Prepare the concrete result first and combine related decisions.
+Respect project guarded commands. Update the report before any commit; developer-run
+commits do not block independent local work.
 
-**Context Gathering:**
+## One findings ledger
 
-- Read-only except for the final write: parse input, fetch tracker/Confluence context, check for an approved design (`solution/` folder), then stop and confirm the combined summary with the developer before writing anything.
-- Persist the confirmed summary once as `intent.md` — a small proto-spec (problem, proposed outcome, affected users/systems, constraints, open questions). Never rewrite its confirmed sections afterward; only append to Open Questions.
-- Creates the story folder and the `2-report.md` skeleton (empty Progress table) — no other stage creates these.
-- Guards against a direct re-invocation clobbering an existing `intent.md`: offer overwrite/stop rather than silently rewriting confirmed intent.
+`2-report.md` contains one `## Review Findings` table, defined by
+`dev/patterns/review-gate.md`. Plan audits, implementation reviews, PR reviews, HLD
+audits and documentation consistency reviews upsert stable RF IDs. A recurring issue
+keeps one row and accumulates origin/evidence. Kind, deviation type, severity,
+classification and resolution are separate dimensions. Record before applying fixes.
 
-**Ceremony:**
+The deviation audit compares actual implementation to HLD contracts, boundaries and
+NFRs only. LLD lag before Document is a normal doc-update task. A contradiction left
+after updates is a docs finding. Target decisions are not silently rewritten to excuse
+implementation regressions. Read the active HLD version through its README index.
 
-- Tracker setup and branch checkout only — no reading or writing of intent/plan content.
-- Ticket-tracker activity is entirely `@scrum-master`'s responsibility; this stage only asks it to act by state name ("transition to In Progress"), never names a tracker or a transition ID itself.
+Tech Debt remains a separate linked ledger for ownership, next action and optional
+tracker task creation. A local TD entry can survive declined optional tracker creation;
+it cannot silently waive required acceptance criteria. Before archival every finding
+must be fixed, accepted, tech-debt or doc-updated with evidence and required attributed
+decisions. Critical/high risks cannot be hidden in debt or accepted silently.
 
-**Plan:**
+## Documentation and completion
 
-- Dedicated to planning only: reads `intent.md` (and any `solution/` files it references) plus the codebase — it does not gather context or run tracker/branch ceremony itself.
-- All Target Architecture reads go through the README to resolve the active version — never hardcode a version name. Read `System Overview.md`, relevant `Containers/<Name>.md` files, and `Non-Functional Concerns/` within that version.
-- Read System Architecture (LLD) before proposing anything.
-- If an approved design exists (`solution/` folder for the ticket), use it as the primary spec. Tracker ACs supplement; they do not override the solution.
-- **Default Step 1 — TDD.** Unless the developer opts out, the project has no established test convention, or the ticket has no testable code path, the plan's Step 1 is "write tests for the Acceptance Criteria" using the project's existing test framework — failing before implementation, passing after. Later steps' verification includes the corresponding AC test(s) passing.
-- **Architecture audit (optional):** for non-trivial plans — new cross-layer integration, infra/IAM change, data-flow change, or multi-NX-project scope — audit the plan against the Target Architecture before saving. Uses the satellite-review pattern. Violations require rework or justification. Skip for mechanical plans (single-layer rename, config value, dependency bump).
-- Record justified deviations in `1-plan.md` under `## Architecture Deviations`.
-- `1-plan.md` is immutable once saved — never edited after creation.
-- The plan is designed and approved inside Claude Code's native Plan Mode (`EnterPlanMode`/`ExitPlanMode`), not a manual write-confirm loop. Plan Mode restricts writes to its own session-scoped plan file; once approved, the identical content is persisted to `1-plan.md` in the story folder — that copy, not the session plan file, is what later stages read.
+Read project documentation principles and placement rules. Include implemented impacts
+from approved design in the same update list, then update app READMEs, LLD and Engineering
+Guide as appropriate. HLD changes require settled authorized target decisions; routine
+LLD updates describe actual built behavior. Review modified docs for contradictions and
+stale references. Resolve new findings before closure; escalate after three unsuccessful
+review/fix rounds instead of looping indefinitely.
 
-**Implement:**
+Archive preserves all story artifacts, including `impl/stat.json`. Never overwrite an
+archive destination. The full-flow router owns tracker completion exactly once and
+keeps lifecycle metrics unfinished while required external completion work remains.
+Direct-stage entry reports only its own result; local IDs skip tracker worklogs/transitions.
 
-- Execute one step at a time. Hard stop after each step — do not write any file until the developer confirms verification passed.
-- After verification: follow the **do → report → commit** pattern — update `2-report.md` first (progress row, implementation note, efforts row), then present the commit message, then wait for commit confirmation before starting the next step.
-- Surface architecture deviations from the plan at the start of the phase.
-- **Satellite review:** after completing any non-trivial step, the worker agent invokes `@architect` as a read-only reviewer before presenting verification. Verdict is go or reiterate. Maximum 3 iterations; escalate to the developer if unresolved. Skip for mechanical steps (rename, config value, dependency bump).
-- **Implementation notes:** if a step passed first try, a one-liner is enough. If validation surfaced errors or required multi-step troubleshooting, write a full incident record — initial error, each hypothesis ruled out, final root cause and fix. A terse "fixed" entry is not acceptable for a troubleshooting chain. Notes added at the bottom, in ascending step order.
-- **TD triage:** when the developer resolves a tech debt item now, invoke `/dev plan` but skip straight to plan-content writing (bypass the idempotency check and intent re-read — context is already established). Append TD steps to the existing `1-plan.md`.
+## Shared patterns
 
-**Test:**
+| Pattern | Purpose |
+| --- | --- |
+| `approvals.md` | Material decisions and authorization boundaries across the flow |
+| `review-gate.md` | Stable finding identity, classification and evidence-backed closure |
+| `do-report-commit.md` | Verify and update the report before any authorized commit |
+| `write-confirm.md` | Batch routine doc edits; ask only for unresolved decisions |
+| `satellite-review.md` | Scoped architecture review with at most three fix/review rounds |
+| `announce-progress.md` | Concise progress at completed units and stage transitions |
+| `session-continuity.md` | Resume current state and authorization without replaying work |
+| `task-tracking.md` | Six stage tasks and implementation step tasks, with tool fallback |
+| `metrics.md` | Observed timing, checks, token evidence and quality inventory |
 
-- Check the build before running tests. Do not run tests against a broken build.
-- Validate each acceptance criterion explicitly — do not assume pass from "tests are green".
-- Include a layer-delegated PR review using the **review-gate** pattern: write all findings to `2-report.md` first, classify each finding, stop for developer confirmation, then apply fixes one at a time (each fix follows the do → report → commit loop).
-- **@architect audit:** for any plan touching infrastructure, introducing a new cross-layer integration, or spanning more than one container — spawn `@architect` (read-only) to audit against HLD boundaries, NFRs, and layer best practices before writing the PR Review table.
+Patterns are companions under `.claude/skills/dev/patterns/`; stage references own their
+trigger conditions. Keep the shared contract in the pattern, not repeated local overrides.
 
-**Document:**
+## Delivery and quality metrics
 
-- Mandatory. The ticket is not complete until this phase runs and the story is archived.
-- Resolve every architecture deviation: update Target Architecture or create a tech debt ticket.
-- Update each documentation item using the **write-confirm** pattern — write the file, ask for review, stop, wait for confirmation before the next item.
-- **Deviation audit:** before classifying what to document, read both `1-plan.md` and `2-report.md` in full, merge the context, and feed it to `@architect` (read-only) to surface every decision — planned or emergent — that diverges from or is absent from the Target Architecture and LLD docs. Uses the **review-gate** pattern: write findings to `2-report.md` as `## Deviation Audit`, stop, confirm, then proceed.
-- **Satellite consistency review:** after all doc updates, spawn `@architect` (read-only) to cross-check all modified docs for contradictions and stale references. Uses the **review-gate** pattern with tri-choice: fix / tech-debt ticket / skip.
-- **Placement:** use the HLD/LLD matrix to decide where each change lands. HLD hit → update the relevant HLD container or NFR doc (settled outcome only) and record detail in the LLD. HLD miss → create a minimal new HLD entry and capture full detail in the LLD.
+Each ticket keeps `impl/stat.json` beside `2-report.md`. The dependency-free Node.js
+CLI `scripts/dev-metrics.mjs` requires an explicit `--dir` and records observed work,
+waits, attempts, verification outcomes and available runtime token deltas. Unknown
+measurements remain null. Recovery bounds interrupted work at its last checkpoint.
+Direct-stage coverage is partial; the router finalizes full-flow completion metrics.
 
----
+`report` derives `quality` from Review Findings, Tech Debt and numerical Test Results
+and renders one summary line beside Stage Metrics. Breakdowns cover kind, deviation
+type, impact severity, classification, resolution, PR-origin findings and debt disposition.
+Written tests are new cases from the diff; Passed/Failed/Skipped are latest runner case
+counts over non-overlapping scopes. Historical failed test runs are separate from case
+counts. Unknown counts are unavailable; repeat report generation does not increment them.
+These are recorded inventories, not a quality score or an unqualified ticket ranking.
 
-## Patterns
-
-Patterns are shared multi-step protocols co-located in `.claude/skills/dev/patterns/`. They are not registered in `AGENTS.md` — each stage reference loads them on-demand via explicit path reference. The pattern file is the single source of truth for the protocol; the stage reference owns only the trigger condition and any local overrides.
-
-| Pattern                  | File                       | What it enforces                                                                                                                                                                  | Applied in                                                                       |
-| ------------------------ | --------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
-| **do → report → commit** | `do-report-commit.md`      | Update `2-report.md` before presenting any commit message. Report and commit history must stay in sync.                                                                           | Implement (per step), review-gate Stage 2 (per fix), Document (phase wrap-up)     |
-| **review-gate**          | `review-gate.md`           | Write all agent findings to `2-report.md` first → classify → STOP → per-fix loop with individual validation. Never apply a fix before the developer sees the full findings table. | Test (PR review), Document (deviation audit, satellite review)                   |
-| **write-confirm**        | `write-confirm.md`         | Write the file to disk before asking for approval. Developer reviews the artifact in their editor, not in chat. Loop until explicitly confirmed.                                  | Document (per doc item)                                                          |
-| **announce-progress**    | `announce-progress.md`     | After each completed unit: `✅ Done / 🔜 Next in this phase / 📋 After this phase`. Keeps scope visible mid-session and surfaces omissions before they become regressions.        | Implement (after each step), Document (after each item), phase transitions in `/dev` |
-| **satellite-review**     | `satellite-review.md`      | Worker agent invokes `@architect` (read-only) after completing a step. Verdict: go or reiterate. Max 3 iterations; escalate to developer if unresolved.                           | Implement (worker agents — non-trivial steps), Plan (architecture audit — optional) |
-| **session-continuity**   | `session-continuity.md`    | On resume after compaction: re-read the current stage reference in full. On stage exit: re-read `dev/SKILL.md` and resume the router from the next stage.                         | All six stage references                                                         |
-| **task-tracking**        | `task-tracking.md`         | Native `TaskCreate`/`TaskUpdate`/`TaskList` (with `TodoWrite`/report-only fallback) over an ordered unit list, `2-report.md` as the durable source of truth on resume.            | `/dev` router (one task per stage), Implement (one task per plan step)           |
-
-Plan's design-and-approve step now uses Claude Code's native Plan Mode
-(`EnterPlanMode`/`ExitPlanMode`) instead of the write-confirm pattern — see Invariants
-above.
-
-**Principles:**
-
-- Extract a pattern when 3+ call sites share the same multi-step protocol.
-- Co-locate under `.claude/skills/dev/patterns/` — not in `AGENTS.md` registry, not in `skills/drafts/`.
-- Reference by explicit file path at the point of use in the stage reference.
-- The pattern owns the rule text; the stage reference owns the trigger condition and any local overrides.
-- Update the pattern file only when the protocol itself evolves — not for local variations.
